txc (0.2.0) experimental; urgency=low

  * Reorganise the project around a registry of text operations, from which
    the command line parser, the help text, the shell completions and the
    interactive interface are all generated.
  * Add 143 operations across ten categories: case conversion, encoding,
    hashing, line editing, text cleanup, number formats, format conversion,
    inspection, generators and time.
  * Accept input as arguments, from a file or over a pipe, with the same
    result in each case.
  * Add an interactive full screen interface, shown when txc is run with no
    arguments, with live output as you type.
  * Add shell completion scripts for bash, zsh, fish, powershell and elvish.
  * Replace the panics on invalid input with reported errors and a non zero
    exit status.

 -- Matheus Santos <vorj.dux@gmail.com>  Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

